1
00:00:34,011 --> 00:00:37,051
WHY DO YOU CONTINUE TO FORGET US?
WHY HAVE YOU ABANDONED US FOR SO LONG?

2
00:00:37,141 --> 00:00:38,261
God,

3
00:00:40,351 --> 00:00:42,561
do we really

4
00:00:42,641 --> 00:00:44,771
have to be pure?

5
00:00:51,151 --> 00:00:52,321
Really?

6
00:00:53,241 --> 00:00:56,071
My father said that those who do not
follow your commands

7
00:00:56,161 --> 00:00:58,121
shall be punished.

8
00:01:02,041 --> 00:01:03,701
Even if they're an angel.

9
00:01:06,171 --> 00:01:08,081
A person like me

10
00:01:08,171 --> 00:01:10,461
could never understand your will.

11
00:01:11,801 --> 00:01:15,591
But I feel that your kingdom in heaven

12
00:01:15,671 --> 00:01:18,011
is very far away.

13
00:01:19,051 --> 00:01:20,391
Anne!

14
00:01:21,601 --> 00:01:24,521
Help me get dinner ready!

15
00:01:24,601 --> 00:01:26,941
I'm coming! I'm coming!

16
00:01:40,071 --> 00:01:41,121
I felt burdened

17
00:01:42,951 --> 00:01:44,661
to know that

18
00:01:46,911 --> 00:01:49,291
you sit in heaven

19
00:01:50,791 --> 00:01:54,051
and watch us.

20
00:03:27,471 --> 00:03:28,471
THE LIGHT OF DAWN

21
00:03:28,601 --> 00:03:29,641
Jehovah.

22
00:03:30,771 --> 00:03:33,691
Restore us to yourself,

23
00:03:33,771 --> 00:03:35,771
oh, Lord,

24
00:03:37,111 --> 00:03:38,691
that we may return,

25
00:03:40,281 --> 00:03:42,281
renew our days

26
00:03:43,241 --> 00:03:46,491
as of old.

27
00:03:53,461 --> 00:03:56,591
Oh, it's like this, Mr. Priest.

28
00:03:57,291 --> 00:03:58,501
That's it!

29
00:03:58,591 --> 00:04:00,511
It's like me and my brother.

30
00:04:01,551 --> 00:04:04,431
We've always been together since we were kids.

31
00:04:04,511 --> 00:04:06,641
We helped each other out.

32
00:04:08,601 --> 00:04:11,021
Our teamwork makes us unbeatable

33
00:04:11,101 --> 00:04:13,771
on the battlefield. Right?

34
00:04:14,901 --> 00:04:17,521
Yeah. We can read each other's minds.

35
00:04:17,611 --> 00:04:20,901
He's the only one I can trust to have my back.

36
00:04:20,991 --> 00:04:25,661
I'd never trade our relationship for silver.
Right, brother?

37
00:04:25,741 --> 00:04:29,871
Of course not, brother. Well, it depends on how much.

38
00:04:31,701 --> 00:04:34,041
It's a bond of brotherhood!

39
00:04:34,961 --> 00:04:36,961
-What do you think?
-What do you think?

40
00:04:37,711 --> 00:04:39,841
-Did we get it right?
-Did we get it right?

41
00:04:40,001 --> 00:04:43,301
Well, who knows?

42
00:04:44,841 --> 00:04:47,931
It's completely different from what I imagine love to be.

43
00:04:49,761 --> 00:04:52,061
Listen, you priest.

44
00:04:53,101 --> 00:04:55,441
You've never been on the battlefield.

45
00:04:55,521 --> 00:04:57,771
So, you don't understand
how amazing this is!

46
00:04:57,861 --> 00:05:00,441
A union formed in a moment of life or death!

47
00:05:00,521 --> 00:05:02,741
You'd never be able to do it yourself!

48
00:05:04,781 --> 00:05:07,241
I think it's wonderful.

49
00:05:07,781 --> 00:05:09,531
It must be something very valuable

50
00:05:09,621 --> 00:05:11,951
to you two brothers.

51
00:05:13,201 --> 00:05:14,201
Well then.

52
00:05:15,121 --> 00:05:17,171
If I were to enter the battlefield,

53
00:05:17,831 --> 00:05:20,751
would you have my back?

54
00:05:21,801 --> 00:05:24,051
What? What are you talking about?

55
00:05:24,381 --> 00:05:26,841
I can do it because he's my brother.

56
00:05:26,931 --> 00:05:29,641
I can't trust my back to a drunk priest!

57
00:05:31,261 --> 00:05:32,681
Right?

58
00:05:32,771 --> 00:05:34,271
That's why it's not the same.

59
00:05:34,351 --> 00:05:39,191
Excuse me, could you explain it
in a way I can understand?

60
00:05:39,271 --> 00:05:42,271
Well then, what about you?

61
00:05:42,651 --> 00:05:44,611
You really like booze.

62
00:05:44,691 --> 00:05:47,111
Maybe that's "love."

63
00:05:47,991 --> 00:05:49,241
No.

64
00:05:49,741 --> 00:05:53,491
It's not that I love booze.

65
00:05:53,581 --> 00:05:54,661
What?

66
00:05:54,751 --> 00:05:55,951
Then stop drinking.

67
00:05:56,041 --> 00:05:57,411
I'm sorry.

68
00:05:57,501 --> 00:05:59,921
He doesn't make sense.

69
00:06:00,001 --> 00:06:02,001
You like things that don't make sense?

70
00:06:02,091 --> 00:06:04,251
Then how about this?

71
00:06:05,381 --> 00:06:08,091
The veterans still talk about it even today.

72
00:06:08,721 --> 00:06:12,011
It's a story about when
we attacked a ship in the Faroes.

73
00:06:12,891 --> 00:06:15,721
There was one warrior on that ship.

74
00:06:16,311 --> 00:06:19,231
He had incredible strength.

75
00:06:21,111 --> 00:06:25,191
We attacked him together,

76
00:06:25,281 --> 00:06:27,991
but he beat 30 of our men with his bare hands!

77
00:06:28,071 --> 00:06:29,151
His bare hands!

78
00:06:31,491 --> 00:06:33,871
In the end, we killed him.

79
00:06:33,951 --> 00:06:38,211
But when it was time to count our losses,
we found that no one had died.

80
00:06:38,291 --> 00:06:41,041
I wonder what that was all about.

81
00:06:41,131 --> 00:06:44,091
That guy was carrying a sword, right?

82
00:06:44,171 --> 00:06:47,091
Maybe he thought we were no match for him.

83
00:06:47,171 --> 00:06:49,221
If so, it angers me.

84
00:06:49,301 --> 00:06:51,891
Where are his manners as a warrior?

85
00:06:55,011 --> 00:06:56,101
Did he

86
00:06:57,141 --> 00:06:58,891
do anything else?

87
00:06:59,731 --> 00:07:01,351
What's his name?

88
00:07:01,441 --> 00:07:04,191
I-- I don't know his name.

89
00:07:05,981 --> 00:07:06,981
I guess

90
00:07:07,071 --> 00:07:11,321
weirdos are drawn to each other.

91
00:07:11,411 --> 00:07:14,371
That guy said some strange things, too.

92
00:07:14,451 --> 00:07:17,951
"A true warrior doesn't need a sword."

93
00:07:18,041 --> 00:07:19,371
Something like that.

94
00:07:29,631 --> 00:07:31,511
What? Priest?

95
00:07:31,591 --> 00:07:34,341
Hey. Where are you going? Hey!

96
00:07:39,061 --> 00:07:41,061
What is it, priest?

97
00:07:41,141 --> 00:07:43,651
Did we get it right? Was that "love?"

98
00:07:53,741 --> 00:07:57,201
A warrior... A true...

99
00:07:57,741 --> 00:07:59,951
Doesn't need a sword...

100
00:08:06,711 --> 00:08:09,761
A true warrior...

101
00:08:21,931 --> 00:08:25,441
Don't complain to me about the weather!

102
00:08:26,191 --> 00:08:29,651
I'm a sailor. The weather on top of a hill

103
00:08:29,731 --> 00:08:32,611
is not my area of expertise.

104
00:08:33,201 --> 00:08:36,701
No one could have predicted that it was
going to snow this much

105
00:08:36,781 --> 00:08:38,081
at the start of winter.

106
00:08:38,781 --> 00:08:41,871
That's not what I'm trying to say.

107
00:08:41,951 --> 00:08:45,621
I'm trying to say that luck is no longer on your side.

108
00:08:45,791 --> 00:08:49,501
We changed our route to beat the winter snows,
and now we end up like this!

109
00:08:49,591 --> 00:08:52,841
Your soldiers are also worried.

110
00:08:53,921 --> 00:08:57,011
My men have been to hell and back.

111
00:08:57,261 --> 00:09:00,311
For them, this is nothing.

112
00:09:00,681 --> 00:09:03,731
They're following their orders with no hesitation. See?

113
00:09:07,101 --> 00:09:10,571
Turn back. It'd be crazy to try to cross Mercia!

114
00:09:12,481 --> 00:09:16,611
If we're going to walk through the snow,
we'll have to leave our plunder behind.

115
00:09:16,991 --> 00:09:18,661
My men aren't going to like that.

116
00:09:19,831 --> 00:09:21,121
Either way,

117
00:09:21,201 --> 00:09:23,501
we can't camp out in the open tonight.

118
00:09:26,421 --> 00:09:27,621
Askeladd.

119
00:09:27,711 --> 00:09:29,711
We're ready.

120
00:09:29,791 --> 00:09:31,131
We can go.

121
00:09:31,211 --> 00:09:32,251
All right.

122
00:09:34,091 --> 00:09:35,261
Askeladd.

123
00:09:36,511 --> 00:09:38,391
When luck's not on your side,

124
00:09:38,471 --> 00:09:40,761
no matter what you do,
it's going to backfire.

125
00:09:40,851 --> 00:09:42,181
Ragnar.

126
00:09:44,221 --> 00:09:46,601
What are you hesitating for?

127
00:09:50,111 --> 00:09:53,231
Attacking and plundering villages

128
00:09:54,151 --> 00:09:56,651
is a tradition for us Norsemen.

129
00:10:04,661 --> 00:10:07,331
Our father, who art in heaven,

130
00:10:07,581 --> 00:10:11,591
give us this day our daily bread.

131
00:10:11,841 --> 00:10:14,421
And forgive us our debts,

132
00:10:14,501 --> 00:10:16,721
as we also have forgiven our debtors.

133
00:10:17,761 --> 00:10:19,381
And lead us not into temptation,

134
00:10:19,471 --> 00:10:22,051
but deliver us from evil.

135
00:10:22,141 --> 00:10:24,311
For thine is the kingdom,

136
00:10:24,391 --> 00:10:26,771
and the power, and the glory,
for ever and ever.

137
00:10:27,641 --> 00:10:28,691
Amen.

138
00:10:28,771 --> 00:10:30,021
Amen.

139
00:10:35,941 --> 00:10:37,781
Hey, Father!

140
00:10:38,401 --> 00:10:41,031
Why do we always pray?

141
00:10:42,371 --> 00:10:46,041
Because Jesus told us to do so.

142
00:10:46,121 --> 00:10:48,371
Jesus is always right.

143
00:10:48,751 --> 00:10:51,541
What happens if we don't pray?

144
00:10:51,631 --> 00:10:56,131
Well, the unbelievers are going to go to hell.

145
00:10:56,211 --> 00:10:57,551
That's right.

146
00:10:57,631 --> 00:11:01,891
Hell is a scary place where the devil lives.

147
00:11:01,971 --> 00:11:04,051
You don't want to see the devil, right?

148
00:11:05,471 --> 00:11:07,311
I'm scared of the devil.

149
00:11:07,391 --> 00:11:09,311
Yeah. I'm scared of him, too.

150
00:11:09,891 --> 00:11:13,811
But good kids who pray can go to heaven.

151
00:11:13,901 --> 00:11:15,321
Don't forget.

152
00:11:18,611 --> 00:11:20,901
It doesn't make sense.

153
00:11:21,201 --> 00:11:25,531
Everyone's going to be taken to heaven
or hell soon?

154
00:11:25,621 --> 00:11:29,251
I don't want our family to get separated.

155
00:11:29,331 --> 00:11:31,121
But, Father,

156
00:11:31,211 --> 00:11:35,381
why did God decide to pass judgment
on the world all of a sudden?

157
00:11:35,671 --> 00:11:37,251
It's not sudden.

158
00:11:37,341 --> 00:11:39,631
It was decided a long time ago

159
00:11:39,711 --> 00:11:43,591
that it would happen a thousand years
after the resurrection of Jesus.

160
00:11:44,721 --> 00:11:46,851
In other words, 20 years later.

161
00:11:53,101 --> 00:11:57,321
When God passes judgment,
all evil men are going to hell.

162
00:11:57,981 --> 00:11:59,151
I know!

163
00:11:59,231 --> 00:12:01,111
The Danes are the evil men!

164
00:12:01,191 --> 00:12:03,611
Yeah! They're really evil.

165
00:12:04,071 --> 00:12:07,451
I'm sure God knew that
people like them

166
00:12:07,531 --> 00:12:09,371
would turn up.

167
00:12:09,911 --> 00:12:14,251
Listen. Make sure you follow God's commandments.

168
00:12:15,211 --> 00:12:16,211
Anne.

169
00:12:18,671 --> 00:12:19,801
I have to pee.

170
00:12:28,641 --> 00:12:32,601
What am I going to do? I'm so scared of the devil!

171
00:12:54,751 --> 00:12:56,331
But it's so pretty!

172
00:12:57,751 --> 00:12:59,381
I put it on again.

173
00:13:00,841 --> 00:13:03,721
I wonder how much this ring costs.

174
00:13:03,801 --> 00:13:05,881
I wonder if God would forgive me

175
00:13:05,971 --> 00:13:08,511
if I paid for it.

176
00:13:12,851 --> 00:13:16,521
The devil must have tempted me.

177
00:13:22,861 --> 00:13:27,111
I shouldn't have gone to the market
when I don't have any money.

178
00:13:30,121 --> 00:13:32,451
I bet bad children like me

179
00:13:32,541 --> 00:13:35,791
will be sent to hell
on the day of judgment.

180
00:13:38,041 --> 00:13:40,961
I bet I'm going to be the only one
in my family

181
00:13:42,381 --> 00:13:44,091
who's not going to heaven.

182
00:13:58,851 --> 00:14:00,481
Wow!

183
00:14:00,561 --> 00:14:03,481
It looks so pretty on my left hand, too!

184
00:14:10,491 --> 00:14:11,491
Who are they?

185
00:14:16,541 --> 00:14:17,961
What's wrong with your face?

186
00:14:18,961 --> 00:14:22,001
Me, too! Me, too!

187
00:14:23,171 --> 00:14:25,761
Weren't you listening just now?

188
00:14:25,841 --> 00:14:28,721
If you're not good,
God is going to punish you--

189
00:14:35,221 --> 00:14:37,141
Hey.

190
00:14:37,231 --> 00:14:38,981
I found dinner.

191
00:14:40,021 --> 00:14:44,941
BUT THOU HAST UTTERLY REJECTED US;
THOU ART VERY WROTH AGAINST US.

192
00:14:48,531 --> 00:14:49,951
Everyone!

193
00:14:50,031 --> 00:14:51,871
Run away!

194
00:14:51,951 --> 00:14:55,121
The village is under attack!

195
00:14:55,201 --> 00:14:56,201
The Danes

196
00:14:56,291 --> 00:14:57,911
are attacking the village!

197
00:14:59,121 --> 00:15:00,211
Shut up!

198
00:15:07,341 --> 00:15:09,471
It's so warm here. I feel alive again.

199
00:15:09,551 --> 00:15:12,341
What's with this family?
There's so many kids.

200
00:15:14,181 --> 00:15:17,311
What do you want all of a sudden?

201
00:15:17,391 --> 00:15:20,771
Milk porridge with barley and a bit of jerky.

202
00:15:20,851 --> 00:15:22,941
It has onions in it.

203
00:15:23,861 --> 00:15:26,401
Hey. Get everything that can be used
as a weapon.

204
00:15:26,481 --> 00:15:27,481
Okay.

205
00:15:35,411 --> 00:15:38,661
This is terrible. You're eating some bad food.

206
00:15:41,331 --> 00:15:43,921
Hey! What's wrong with you?

207
00:15:44,001 --> 00:15:45,591
Don't waste food!

208
00:15:45,671 --> 00:15:47,881
-Mom!
-You're going to be punished for this!

209
00:15:54,091 --> 00:15:56,141
Are you okay? Hey!

210
00:15:56,221 --> 00:15:59,851
How do you say it in English again?

211
00:15:59,931 --> 00:16:02,061
"Give me all your food."

212
00:16:02,141 --> 00:16:04,351
Yes. That's right.

213
00:16:04,441 --> 00:16:07,231
-Hey!
-Hey, old man.

214
00:16:11,031 --> 00:16:14,451
Give me all your food. I'll kill you.

215
00:16:19,041 --> 00:16:20,581
And this one.

216
00:16:24,461 --> 00:16:25,631
Is that all?

217
00:16:27,291 --> 00:16:28,341
Put it there.

218
00:16:28,751 --> 00:16:31,551
If we count two kids as one adult,
that makes 50 people.

219
00:16:31,631 --> 00:16:34,801
That means there's only enough food for 50
to last the winter.

220
00:16:40,771 --> 00:16:43,231
It won't be enough for 104 soldiers.

221
00:16:47,021 --> 00:16:48,861
What am I going to do?

222
00:16:48,941 --> 00:16:51,861
They captured everyone! What am I going to do?

223
00:16:56,031 --> 00:16:57,371
Hey, Priest!

224
00:16:59,831 --> 00:17:02,121
You're the prince's teacher.

225
00:17:02,201 --> 00:17:04,621
That makes you our guest.

226
00:17:05,921 --> 00:17:07,541
I'll forgive you just once.

227
00:17:07,631 --> 00:17:09,881
But if you get in our way again,

228
00:17:09,961 --> 00:17:11,671
I'm going to kill you on the spot.

229
00:17:12,921 --> 00:17:15,301
I hate priests, to be honest.

230
00:17:18,221 --> 00:17:20,141
Are you guys

231
00:17:21,721 --> 00:17:23,521
Danes?

232
00:17:23,601 --> 00:17:26,351
Do any of you speak our language?

233
00:17:35,241 --> 00:17:38,361
I beg you! Leave us half of the food!

234
00:17:38,451 --> 00:17:41,201
Please, at least leave us half of the food.

235
00:17:41,281 --> 00:17:44,201
If we have half, we can make it through the winter!

236
00:17:48,081 --> 00:17:50,751
I have a baby! Please!

237
00:17:52,711 --> 00:17:55,591
A baby? That's rough.

238
00:17:59,261 --> 00:18:03,221
Don't worry. I made sure to think about you.

239
00:18:03,311 --> 00:18:06,231
You don't have to worry about making it through
the winter.

240
00:18:07,691 --> 00:18:09,731
Really? Really?

241
00:18:10,271 --> 00:18:11,691
It's true.

242
00:18:12,321 --> 00:18:16,441
You don't need to worry about making it through
this winter or any winters to come.

243
00:18:17,571 --> 00:18:20,531
I'm going to release you from your suffering.

244
00:18:25,951 --> 00:18:29,541
Askeladd. They're civilians.

245
00:18:31,211 --> 00:18:34,751
Even if I let them live, I don't have any food
to feed them.

246
00:18:35,921 --> 00:18:37,471
If even one of them escapes,

247
00:18:37,551 --> 00:18:40,471
they're going to tell the enemy that we're here.

248
00:18:40,551 --> 00:18:42,391
We can't allow that to happen.

249
00:18:43,681 --> 00:18:46,021
How did it go? Were you able to dig the hole?

250
00:18:46,101 --> 00:18:49,601
Yeah. We can fit 62 if we cram them in.

251
00:18:49,691 --> 00:18:50,731
Askeladd!

252
00:18:51,441 --> 00:18:53,821
They're Christians!

253
00:18:54,611 --> 00:18:56,111
So what?

254
00:18:56,731 --> 00:19:00,201
This is what's best for the prince.

255
00:19:00,661 --> 00:19:01,661
All right.

256
00:19:01,781 --> 00:19:03,241
Any more questions?

257
00:19:04,581 --> 00:19:06,041
No more questions.

258
00:19:06,291 --> 00:19:07,451
Very well.

259
00:19:07,701 --> 00:19:08,791
Men!

260
00:19:11,671 --> 00:19:12,791
Kill them.

261
00:20:58,861 --> 00:21:00,111
God.

262
00:21:02,901 --> 00:21:06,491
Are you watching?

263
00:21:16,331 --> 00:21:17,791
Did my father,

264
00:21:17,881 --> 00:21:20,341
my mother, my grandfather,

265
00:21:20,421 --> 00:21:22,421
my brothers, and my sisters

266
00:21:26,841 --> 00:21:29,011
arrive over there?

267
00:21:43,941 --> 00:21:48,071
You aren't going to call me there too, right?

268
00:21:49,531 --> 00:21:50,741
Right?

269
00:21:51,911 --> 00:21:53,411
Because

270
00:21:56,711 --> 00:21:58,621
I feel elated now.

271
00:22:05,211 --> 00:22:06,841
I can't believe

272
00:22:06,921 --> 00:22:10,681
such evil people exist.

273
00:22:12,011 --> 00:22:13,721
I can't believe

274
00:22:13,811 --> 00:22:17,141
there are people who aren't afraid
of your punishment.

275
00:22:21,061 --> 00:22:24,191
Just like the moment I stole this ring.

276
00:22:26,401 --> 00:22:27,991
I feel

277
00:22:32,031 --> 00:22:33,701
elated now.
